          "source_text_sha256": "4575d9ba8887e908d3de32ccbae33ac77f09b8a16e1765b4609b09b3fb34aebd",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: A witness reports their observation made during the night from Sunday to Monday, July 14, 2008 (between midnight and 00:05) in a clear and cloudless sky. They observed above their home the silent passage SO-NE of a large, dark triangular shape bordered at each end by non-flashing round lights, of great size and yellow-orange in color. The witness steps outside but the PAN has disappeared. Only one testimony was collected. Considering the following objective elements:\n\n• Fine weather, good visibility, pitch black night.\n• Light breeze, the trajectory of the PAN is consistent with the direction of the local wind.\n• Short duration observation.\n• The witness saw several large lights with the perception of a single object.\n• Dark orange color, relatively moderate light intensity of the PAN.\n• The observation was made during a 3-day weekend coinciding with a national holiday.\n\nIt is concluded that the witness very likely observed several Thai lanterns (or luminous festive balloons) carried aloft by the wind, giving the impression of a single object. These lanterns could have been launched either from Saint-Malo itself, or from Dinard or one of its beaches on a summer Sunday evening, the eve of a national holiday. The GEIPAN classifies the case as A: Observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "efae6a307f68caa1d0831aa37f7d486f07ce8e6650d95de3be027620bad9948e"
        }
      ],
